    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "    Set within EmberFest’s spirit of community-made magic, this session blends low-tech creativity with bold self-expression. The model brings glamour, playfulness, and embodied storytelling; participants bring pencils, curiosity, and their own artistic “portals of possibility.”  This gathering highlights diversity, celebration of self, and the power of art to envision futures where everyone shines.  Materials required: bring your own sketchbook and drawing medium of choice (pens, pencil, etc.)        &nbsp;    This event:    Offers a safe, inclusive space for art-making.     Encourages playful, imaginative sketching without pressure or perfectionism.    Creates a moment of cross-disciplinary creativity (visual art + performance).    Supports a community culture of respect, celebration, and curiosity.        Drop in entry! No registration is required.    Donations are appreciated and go towards KHC programming.    "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
