    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "      Whether you’re a practiced storyteller, a first-time sharer, or simply someone who loves to listen, this night celebrates creativity, connection, and the everyday magic of gathering together. It’s a small, intimate way to help spark the larger EmberFest spirit: creativity, shared meaning, and low-tech community magic.        Our theme is Positive Futurisms: Portals of Possibility    Participants can sign up to share:      A personal story    A fictional tale or myth    A poem, spoken word piece, or micro-story    For the sake of keeping the event flowing, we ask that your piece is kept between 5 - 10 minutes.    Drop in entry! No registration is required.    Donations are appreciated and go towards KHC programming."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "EmberFest Story Night at Four Points Books"
      }
    ],
