    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Edmonton's beloved prairie-indie trio, Scenic Route to Alaska, has solidified their musical legacy with six acclaimed albums, culminating in the eagerly awaited release of their seventh opus, \"Lasts Forever,\" in April 2024. Throughout their journey characterized by infectious melodies and introspective storytelling, Trevor Mann, Shea Connor, and Murray Wood have continually evolved, garnering numerous accolades along the way.    Their hit single \"Love Keeps\" soared to a SOCAN #1 spot, dominating the CBC Radio 2 charts in 2016. This milestone set the stage for subsequent triumphs, including the prestigious Western Canadian Music Award for Rock Group of the Year in 2018. The band's influence extends beyond the music charts, with five Edmonton Music Awards further cementing their cultural impact.    As \"Lasts Forever\" takes center stage, Scenic Route to Alaska stays true to their prairie-indie roots and electrifying live performances. This latest album showcases a refined sound, drawing upon past influences while venturing into new sonic territories.    With its release, \"Lasts Forever\" captivates audiences with its poignant melodies and thought-provoking lyrics, reinforcing Scenic Route to Alaska's status as pioneers of the Canadian music scene. Their dedication to their craft and unwavering passion continue to resonate with fans worldwide, ensuring their legacy endures for years to come."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "KHC presents: Scenic Route to Alaska"
      }
    ],
