    "https://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-us",
        "@value": "AGOG presents: Prey to Gather by Shasta McCoy | Kicking Horse Culture"
      }
    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-us",
        "@value": "Shasta McCoy is a fiber artist who engages wool as a textile and sculptural medium along with wood, stone, metal, found objects and other fibers. Shasta’s relationship with fiber wool extends back to her childhood in east Tennessee on a small farm with sheep where she was active in 4-H and will forever be the 1994 Tennessee Sheep and Wool Queen. Shasta lives in Golden, the traditional territory of the Secwépemc and Ktunaxa Nations, where her art practice intertwines witchcraft and mythos. Her work explores archetypes of the divine feminine/masculine, cyclical rhythms, healing, and connection to land and water."
      }
    ],
