    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carl Trinkwon &amp; the \"Masters of Nun\"  Carl Trinkwon and the \"Masters of Nun\" are a Golden band that have been creating and performing a combination of Folk, Blues and original music since 2010. The band features Todd Keith on mandolin, Ian Rowe on violin, and Mike Garner on Bass, as well as Carl on guitar &amp; vocals.The album \"Heart Shock-Ra\" from 2014 displays a collection of gypsy, country and original tunes. Carl is also a solo artist/songwriter with 2 previous albums - \"Cowboys &amp; Secrets\" 1999 and \"Weapons of Peace\" 2004.  Katie Martha and the Other Guys  Katie, Martha and the Other Guys met at the Wolf’s Den pub open mic jam in Golden, BC, where they discovered a natural affinity for playing music together. They landed their first gig at the Eagle’s Eye Restaurant, Kicking Horse Mountain Resort in March 2023. Since then, they have continued to play together whenever their busy schedules allow, sharing their music with  appreciative audiences around Golden, including summer shows at the Golden Skybridge and Golden Summer Kicks Concert Series, and in Revelstoke as part of the Revy Live Outside summer concerts. The band consists of Katie Kendall on lead vocals, piano and guitar, Jackson Baker on bass and backing vocals, John Jenkins on drums and backing vocals, and Todd Keith on mandolin, guitar and backing vocals. They play an entertaining mix of heartfelt ballads and toe-tapping crowd pleasers, covering songs from roots and folk artists such as Chris Stapleton, Gillian Welch, Watchhouse (Mandolin Orange), Gregory Alan Isakov, Elvis Presley and more.  Eric Larocque  Confluence Jazz  Confluence Jazz is a band from Golden BC. They enjoy the creative process, morphing fine music to create a new sound. For them, jazz is a genre without borders. Lead singer and keyboard player Molly Roth is originally from Los Angeles. Molly is joined by Joan Dolinsky on trumpet and keys, Jeff Dolinsky on saxophone, Michael Garner, on upright bass, and Cole Burns on drums."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "KHC presents: Local&#8217;s Night"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://kickinghorseculture.ca/events/ayla-tesler-mabe/",
    "https://ogp.me/ns#locale": [
